[?2004hroot@b07d987c46b4:/task/work# cat /task/input/core_notes.md
[?2004l# Sequencing core hand-over: run 214, panel CGP-22

## Assay

- Hybrid-capture panel CGP-22: 13 target regions, 46.3 kb in total (`targets.bed`). The panel
  reference `reference/ref.fa` (contig `chr22_panel`) is the hg38 chr22 slice the baits were designed on.
- Libraries: enzymatic end repair / A-tailing, ligation of dual-indexed adapters, PCR amplification,
  one pooled capture reaction for all six libraries.
- Sequencing: NovaSeq 6000, flow cell HKF3WDSX7 lane 2, 2 x 100 cycles. Demultiplexed with bcl2fastq;
  adapters were trimmed by the instrument software. FASTQ files are otherwise as produced.
- Requested mean depth on target: tumour 180x, normal 90x.

## Libraries

| sample_id | specimen | DNA input (ng) | shearing | PCR cycles | i7+i5 index |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| CG24-7410 | fresh-frozen biopsy | 80 | batch A | 8 | CTCTATAC+AAATAGAA |
| CG24-1366 | peripheral blood (EDTA) | 200 | batch A | 8 | CTAATGAC+TGTGTCGA |
| CG24-6425 | peripheral blood (EDTA) | 200 | batch A | 8 | GGCATGTG+TCGCCCTT |
| CG24-4187 | fresh-frozen biopsy | 100 | batch A | 8 | CATTAACT+CACGCTGT |
| CG24-9024 | FFPE section (block from 2018) | 80 | batch A | 10 | TAAGTGTC+TGCTGTGG |
| CG24-3973 | peripheral blood (EDTA) | 200 | batch A | 8 | GCCACTTC+TCACTCCC |

## Remarks

- Shearing: Covaris LE220, low-EDTA TE, standard setting, one batch.
- FFPE sections were deparaffinised and extracted with the FFPE DNA kit of the pathology lab.
- Tumour cell content estimated by the pathologist on the adjacent H&E section: PT-0452 70%, PT-0740 60%, PT-0760 70%.
- All libraries passed the core's yield and fragment-size checks (mean insert 260-280 bp).
[?2004hroot@b07d987c46b4:/task/work# python3 -c "open('check_strand.py', 'w').write('''import pysam\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\npairs = [\n    ('PT-0452', 'CG24-4187', 'CG24-1366'),\n    ('PT-0740', 'CG24-7410', 'CG24-6425'),\n    ('PT-0760', 'CG24-9024', 'CG24-3973')\n]\n\ntargets = []\nwith open('/task/input/targets.bed') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        chrom, s, e, name = line.strip().split()[:4]\n        targets.append((chrom, int(s), int(e), name))\n\nref = pysam.FastaFile('ref.fa')\n\nfor pt, t_id, n_id in pairs:\n    print(f'=== {pt} ===')\n    tbam = pysam.AlignmentFile(f'{t_id}.bam')\n    nbam = pysam.AlignmentFile(f'{n_id}.bam')\n    for chrom, s, e, name in targets:\n        for col in tbam.pileup(chrom, s, e, truncate=True, min_base_quality=15, min_mapping_quality=20):\n            pos = col.reference_pos\n            ref_b = ref.fetch(chrom, pos, pos+1).upper()\n            t_frags = {}\n            for r in col.pileups:\n                aln = r.alignment\n                if aln.is_secondary or aln.is_supplementary: continue\n                qn = aln.query_name\n                is_rev = aln.is_reverse\n                if r.is_del:\n                    call = ('DEL', r.indel)\n                elif r.indel > 0:\n                    call = ('INS', aln.query_sequence[r.query_position+1 : r.query_position+1+r.indel])\n                else:\n                    call = ('SNV', aln.query_sequence[r.query_position].upper())\n                t_frags[qn] = (call, is_rev)\n            alt_fwd = defaultdict(int)\n            alt_rev = defaultdict(int)\n            for call, is_rev in t_frags.values():\n                if is_rev: alt_rev[call] += 1\n                else: alt_fwd[call] += 1\n            all_calls = set(alt_fwd.keys()) | set(alt_rev.keys())\n            tot = len(t_frags)\n            for call in all_calls:\n                c_type, c_val = call\n                if c_type == 'SNV' and c_val == ref_b: continue\n                ct = alt_fwd[call] + alt_rev[call]\n                af = ct / tot if tot else 0\n                if af >= 0.04 and ct >= 4:\n                    fwd = alt_fwd[call]\n                    rev = alt_rev[call]\n                    print(f'{chrom}:{pos+1} {ref_b}->{c_type}:{c_val} AF={af:.3f} ct={ct}/{tot} (fwd={fwd}, rev={rev})')\n''')" && python3 check_strand.py > candidates_strand.txt && head -n 40 candidates_strand.txt
